From: Jan Grulich <jgrulich@redhat.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 13:10:00 +0000
Subject: Bug 2059127 - WebRTC backport: Screen capture: validate and snapshot
 cursor and videocrop metadata r=pehrsons

Cap cursor_meta->size against the negotiated maximum and validate that
bitmap_offset and the bitmap pixel data offset both point within the
metadata region before forming pointers and copying data.

Copy cursor and videocrop metadata headers from shared memory into
local storage before validating and using their fields, so the
producer cannot modify them between validation and use.

This is a simple backport of an WebRTC upstream change.

Upstream commit: 9b33b6c524a185a20586741af262370291000b69

Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319761
Mercurial Revision: https://hg.mozilla.org/mozilla-central/rev/a0efe8bc90331a480e396095c9ebe58b30225cb2
